›niÚiVê4Ø3òÙ-ì zPYµžþÞu™iHÔ¶ü{"rendered":{"html":"<p>GCSL infers local values and selected present-or-future positions. It does\nnot infer every relationship between types. Explicit annotations help you\nstate an intended interface when a program reaches one of these limits.</p>\n<p>The following boundaries affect ordinary programs:</p>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Boundary</th><th>What to write</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td>An empty list has no independent element type</td><td>Give it an annotation or an expected <code>List&lt;T&gt;</code> type</td></tr>\n<tr><td>A pure function does not preserve arbitrary future shapes</td><td>Write the present or future contract explicitly</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Recursive impure results can retain a deferred possibility</td><td>Use <code>Present&lt;T&gt;</code> when the result must be present</td></tr>\n<tr><td>General type parameters and intersections are unsupported</td><td>Write concrete structural types</td></tr>\n<tr><td>There is no <code>None</code> value or optional-type shorthand</td><td>Represent alternatives using supported union members</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Narrowing recognizes a plain name tested directly by <code>if</code></td><td>Bind a field to a name before testing it</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Narrowing does not establish facts after an early return</td><td>Keep uses inside the narrowed branch</td></tr>\n<tr><td>A narrowed mutable name is a branch-local copy</td><td>Don't try to update the original through that copy</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>len</code> and <code>show</code> use special call rules</td><td>Call them directly or through supported aliases, rather than storing them as ordinary function values</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p>Expected types reach record fields, call arguments, and other supported\nliteral contexts. An unrelated sibling expression is not a general\nconstraint-solving mechanism. For example, annotate an empty list before\ncombining it with independently inferred values.</p>\n<p>Warnings do not prevent execution. A union inferred from unlike branch\nresults can produce a warning while the program remains valid. Use\n<code>gcsl check</code> to inspect the full set of errors and warnings, and\n<code>gcsl run --dump-types FILE</code> when the inferred shape is unclear.</p>\n<p>These are supported-language boundaries, not promises about a future\ninference engine. The checker implementation and its regression tests\nare the source for the behavior described here.</p>\n","toc":[],"has_mermaid":false,"dangling":[],"warnings":[],"broken":[]},"images":[],"links":{"pages":[],"anchors":[]},"refs":[]}